Annotations - fragments and tagging
description: how a user marks up a document - regions, tag applications, and where they live
- >
  How a user marks up a document: **fragments** (regions) and **annotations** (tags applied to a
  whole node or a fragment). Both live **on the target node** - they travel with the document,
  not in a side file. The user-facing flow is in [annotating](*::server:ui:annotating); companion
  chapters: the [logical graph](*::language:logical-graph) (omni), [metadata](*::meta)
  (`$defs`, `variant`), [pointers](*::language:pointers) (the `::` project scope, `*`/`&`), and
  [queries](*::language:pointers:queries).
- >-
  This model supersedes the old one (a separate `/annotations/*.yo` node per tag application,
  reverse-linked by a `target` pointer). The selector role moves into **fragments**; the
  tag-application becomes a `yamlover-annotations` array element. `$defs: annotation` is redefined and
  `$defs: fragment` is new.
